<article class="env-lemma" id="B1EC7E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B1EC7E">Lemma <span data-tag="B1EC7E">4.2.3.13</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a simplicial set, and let $\calI $ denote the category of simplices of $K$ (as defined above). Then there is a retraction $r: K_{F} \rightarrow K$ which fixes $K \subseteq K_ F$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Given a map $e: \Delta ^ n \rightarrow K_{F}$, we will describe the composite map $r \circ e: \Delta ^ n \rightarrow K$. The map $e$ classifies the following data: 
    <p>
      <ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
A decomposition $[n] = \{ 0, \ldots , i\}  \cup \{ i+1, \ldots , n \} $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii)$"><p>
A map $e_{-}: \Delta ^{i} \rightarrow K$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(iii)$"><p>
A string of morphisms 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \Delta ^{ m_{i+1} } \rightarrow \ldots \rightarrow \Delta ^{ m_ n } \rightarrow K. \]
</div>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(iv)$"><p>
A compatible family of maps $\{  e_ j: \Delta ^{i} \rightarrow \Delta ^{m_ j} \} _{ j > i }$, having the property that each composition $\Delta ^ i \stackrel{e_ j}{\rightarrow } \Delta ^{m_ j} \rightarrow K$ coincide with $e_{-}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul>
    <p>
      If $i = n$, we set $r \circ e = e_{-}$. Otherwise, we let $r \circ e$ denote the composition 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \Delta ^ n \stackrel{f}{\rightarrow } \Delta ^{m_ n} \rightarrow K \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $f: \Delta ^ n \rightarrow \Delta ^{m_ n}$ is defined as follows: 
    <p>
      <ul>
  <li><p>
The restriction $f | \Delta ^{i}$ coincides with $e_ n$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For $i < j \leq n$, we let $f(j)$ denote the image in $\Delta ^{m_ n}$ of the final vertex of $\Delta ^{m_ j}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul>
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>